@section Cursor Chains
@cindex Cursor Chains

@deftp {Class} <cursorchain>
A specialized flexichain that automatically manages cursors using weak pointers for garbage collection.

@table @var
@item cursors
List of weak pointers to cursors associated with this chain
@end table
@end deftp

@deffn {Function} make-cursorchain @t{#!key} (initial-capacity 0) (fill #\_) (min-capacity 5) (expand-factor 1.5)
Creates a new cursorchain with automatic cursor management.

@lisp
(define chain (make-cursorchain))
@end lisp
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} make-cursorchain-left-cursor chain @t{#!key} (position 0)
Creates a left-sticky cursor for @var{chain} and automatically registers it for weak pointer management.

@lisp
(define cursor (make-cursorchain-left-cursor chain :position 1))
@end lisp
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} make-cursorchain-right-cursor chain @t{#!key} (position 0)
Creates a right-sticky cursor for @var{chain} and automatically registers it for weak pointer management.

@lisp
(define cursor (make-cursorchain-right-cursor chain :position 1))
@end lisp
@end deffn
